<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — Ed Chapman"
  description="Privacy on edwardchapman.co.uk: no analytics, no tracking, one functional cookie."
>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p>
    This site has no analytics, tracking scripts, or accounts. Reading it leaves
    no record with me beyond the ordinary request logs Cloudflare processes to
    operate the site. The one cookie this site sets is functional and described
    below.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you use <a href="/ask">Ask about Ed's work</a>, your question is first
    checked against a short list of pre-written answers to common questions; if
    none matches, it is sent to Anthropic to generate an answer, routed through
    Cloudflare's AI Gateway. Either way it is recorded in the site's operational
    logs so abuse of the assistant can be detected; those logs expire
    automatically after a short period. A question that reaches the model is
    also kept, together with the generated answer, in the AI Gateway's request
    log, which holds the most recent 100,000 requests and deletes the oldest
    first — at this site's traffic, entries can stay there for a long time.
    There is no database or account system behind this site. Do not include
    personal or sensitive information in a question.
  </p>
  <p>
    To keep the assistant available to everyone, asking a question that reaches
    the model sets a signed cookie that counts how many questions your browser
    has asked in the past 24 hours. It contains only that count — no identifier
    and no tracking — and is sent only with Ask requests.
  </p>
  <p>
    Questions about any of this:
    <a href="mailto:ed@edwardchapman.co.uk">ed@edwardchapman.co.uk</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
